---
import SiteFooter from '../components/SiteFooter.astro'
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro'
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="How Helping Group began with Helping Homes during the 2019–20 Australian bushfires, and why the service remains ready to activate."
>
  <SiteHeader />
  <main id="main-content">
    <section class="border-b border-forest/10">
      <div class="shell py-18 sm:py-24 lg:py-28">
        <p class="eyebrow">About Helping Group</p>
        <h1 class="display-title display-title--page mt-5">
          A small idea built for a very real need.
        </h1>
        <p class="body-large mt-6 max-w-3xl">
          Helping Group began during the 2019–20 Australian bushfires, when
          thousands of people were making urgent decisions about where they
          could go and what they could take with them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-space bg-white/65">
      <div class="shell grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.7fr_1.3fr] lg:gap-24">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Why it started</p>
          <h2 class="section-title mt-5">Making available help easier to find.</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="space-y-6 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-soft">
          <p>
            The first version of Helping Homes connected people evacuating from
            fires with Australians who had spare accommodation. It grew from a
            direct observation: people wanted to help, but offers spread across
            social media and informal networks were difficult to find at the
            moment they were needed.
          </p>
          <p>
            Helping Group formed around that response. It later explored other
            project ideas, now recorded in the archive, but Helping Homes is the
            organisation’s continuing work.
          </p>
          <p>
            The platform now supports offers of accommodation, paddock space
            and transport. Between emergencies it remains on standby rather
            than pretending there is always an active crisis to respond to.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-space">
      <div class="shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">How we work</p>
        <h2 class="section-title mt-5">Useful before impressive.</h2>
        <div class="mt-10 border-y border-forest/15">
          {[
            [
              'Start with the practical problem',
              'Technology matters only when it makes a difficult situation clearer or helps someone take a useful next step.',
            ],
            [
              'Be explicit about status',
              'A seasonal service should say when it is on standby, when it is activated and when its application is unavailable.',
            ],
            [
              'Respect official boundaries',
              'Helping Homes can connect community support. It does not replace 000, emergency warnings or professional services.',
            ],
          ].map(([title, copy], index) => (
            <article class="grid gap-3 border-b border-forest/10 py-6 last:border-b-0 md:grid-cols-[0.12fr_0.55fr_1fr] md:gap-8">
              <p class="text-sm font-medium text-forest">0{index + 1}</p>
              <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold tracking-[-0.02em] text-ink">{title}</h3>
              <p class="leading-7 text-ink-soft">{copy}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="founder" class="section-space scroll-mt-10 border-t border-forest/10 bg-paper-deep/50">
      <div class="shell grid gap-10 lg:grid-cols-[0.55fr_1.45fr] lg:items-center lg:gap-24">
        <div class="mx-auto flex aspect-square w-full max-w-60 items-center justify-center rounded-xl border border-forest/12 bg-white p-10">
          <img
            src="/icons/hg-colour.png"
            alt="Helping Group"
            width="79"
            height="105"
            class="mx-auto h-full w-auto object-contain"
          />
        </div>
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Founder-led story</p>
          <h2 class="section-title mt-5">Daniel Ferguson</h2>
          <div class="mt-6 space-y-5 text-lg leading-8 text-ink-soft">
            <p>
              Daniel started Helping Homes after seeing the scale of
              displacement during the 2019–20 bushfires and asking whether a
              simple digital service could connect evacuees with spare
              accommodation.
            </p>
            <p>
              Helping Group is kept deliberately focused today: maintain the
              service, be honest about when it is active and make it ready to
              respond when circumstances require it.
            </p>
          </div>
          <a class="button-secondary mt-8" href="mailto:contact@helping.group">
            Contact Helping Group
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>
